# nektos/act configuration for this repo.
#
# The integration workflow provisions LXD, which needs systemd, so it cannot
# run inside act's default Docker containers. Map ubuntu-latest to act's
# "-self-hosted" platform: job steps then run directly on this host, where
# LXD (and everything else the workflow needs) already lives.
#
# act treats a project-level .actrc as untrusted and skips flags that reach
# host resources (like -self-hosted); run act with --trust-project-actrc to
# apply this mapping. See README "Running the CI workflow locally with act".
-P ubuntu-latest=-self-hosted
